{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>The second.</b> From the derivation of 'two,' for the king is as one, and after him the second is like a second to him, and after him the third is like a third." "<b>Chariot.</b> Wood placed upon four horses. And 'his chariot' [as in] מרכבת שלמה לעדה." "<b>Avrech.</b> Every man calls out before him, kneel and bow. This word is from the heavy [pi'el] doubled stem, ויברך על ברכיו (II Chronicles 6:13), from the light [kal] and all from the root ברכים [knees]. And Rabbi Jonah the Spanish grammarian said that avrech is a noun [participle], and the alef stands in place of the heh, like אשכם and שלוח (Jeremiah 25:4). And in my opinion alef in אשכם is the language of the speaker."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:46.764326525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}